---
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
import Icon from "../components/Icon.astro";
import WaveDivider from "../components/WaveDivider.astro";
import ContactSection from "../components/ContactSection.astro";
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Off the clock — Brandon Walker"
  description="The oceans, cities, nature, philosophy, and imaginary worlds that inspire Brandon Walker’s creative work."
>
  <section class="page-heading container">
    <p class="eyebrow">04 / OFF THE CLOCK</p>
    <h1>
      Follow the things
      <br />
      that make you <span class="tide-accent">curious.</span>
    </h1>
    <p>
      A few things that pull me away from the screen. And a few that bring me
      right back.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="page-section container">
    <div class="interest-feature">
      <img
        src="/images/ocean.webp"
        width="1200"
        height="1200"
        alt="Ocean scenery from Brandon’s original portfolio"
      />
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow section-number">01 / OPEN WATER, OPEN MIND</p>
        <h2>
          Drawn to
          <br />
          <span class="tide-accent">the horizon.</span>
        </h2>
        <p>
          The ocean, cruises, and travel. There’s something about open water and
          the promise of a new place that keeps me looking outward.
        </p>
        <p>
          That same sense of possibility finds its way into the digital spaces I
          create.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="interest-grid">
      <article class="interest-tile">
        <span>02 / THE ENERGY OF A CITY</span>
        <h2>Metropolitan possibilities.</h2>
        <p>
          I’m drawn to large cities: the movement, the diversity, and the
          feeling that there’s always another story around the corner. I’m open
          to relocating anywhere in the US.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="interest-tile">
        <span>03 / THE NATURAL WORLD</span>
        <h2>A softer kind of wonder.</h2>
        <p>
          Nature, conservation, and animals. Especially cats. Taking care of the
          real world matters just as much as dreaming up new ones.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="interest-tile">
        <span>04 / THE BIG QUESTIONS</span>
        <h2>Beyond the obvious.</h2>
        <p>
          Philosophy and esoterica keep me curious about how people make
          meaning, see patterns, and imagine what could be.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="interest-tile">
        <span>05 / WORLDS IN PROGRESS</span>
        <h2>Places that don’t exist. Yet.</h2>
        <p>
          3D landscaping in Unreal Engine, Minecraft modding and hosting, web
          development, and digital spaces. I like turning an idea into somewhere
          you can go.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
    <a class="text-link" style="margin-top:30px" href="/work?category=Worlds">
      Explore the worlds I’m building <Icon name="diagonal" size={17} />
    </a>
  </section>
  <WaveDivider />
  <ContactSection />
</SiteLayout>
